description:
Write a model of the `LISTBOX` control's most used messages, with their real return values:

```cpp
constexpr int LB_ERR = -1;

class ListBox
{
public:
    explicit ListBox(bool sorted);                    // LBS_SORT
    int addString(const std::string& s);              // LB_ADDSTRING: the index it went to
    int insertString(int index, const std::string& s);// LB_INSERTSTRING: -1 appends; never sorts
    int deleteString(int index);                      // LB_DELETESTRING: the new count, or LB_ERR
    int getCount() const;
    int getCurSel() const;                            // LB_ERR when nothing is selected
    int setCurSel(int index);                         // -1 clears the selection and returns LB_ERR; a bad index returns LB_ERR
    std::string getText(int index) const;             // "" for a bad index
    int findString(int start, const std::string& prefix) const;   // LB_FINDSTRING
};
```

- A **sorted** list box inserts with `addString` at its place in case-insensitive order (after equal strings).
- Deleting the selected item clears the selection; deleting an item before it moves the selection up by one. Inserting before the selection moves it down.
- `findString` finds the first item that **starts with** `prefix`, ignoring case, searching from the item **after** `start` to the end and then from the beginning, up to and including `start`; `start = -1` searches the whole list from the top. It returns `LB_ERR` if there is no match.

